1
00:00:01,800 --> 00:00:07,144
In Bangladesh, rice is the
staple crop, grown on small family farms.

2
00:00:07,274 --> 00:00:13,314
When a leaf turns sick, there is often no expert nearby,
and advice is rarely in plain Bangla.

3
00:00:13,444 --> 00:00:21,124
The Bangladesh Rice Research Institute warns that blast can
cut yield by up to eighty percent, and bacterial leaf blight by about thirty.

4
00:00:21,254 --> 00:00:27,943
Rice diseases threaten harvests wherever rice
is grown. A wrong guess means the wrong spray and lost money.

5
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:33,884
Meet Kakatarua, the scarecrow that watches your field.

6
00:00:34,015 --> 00:00:40,904
A farmer photographs one rice leaf. AI
suggests the disease, or honestly says it is not sure.

7
00:00:41,034 --> 00:00:47,749
Advice comes only from official rice research factsheets, in
plain Bangla, every step with its source.

8
00:00:47,879 --> 00:00:54,638
It never invents a dose, never names a pesticide, and no outbreak
alert reaches farmers until a human approves it.

9
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,570
This is the live app: Bangla
first, English one tap away, with read-aloud.

10
00:01:05,700 --> 00:01:15,779
The farmer picks a division, never an exact location, and takes
a photo. GPS data is removed, and blurry photos are refused before any AI call.

11
00:01:15,909 --> 00:01:23,448
Meta's Muse Spark model must choose from nine
rice diseases. Here it found brown spot, with medium confidence.

12
00:01:23,578 --> 00:01:33,303
The farmer gets five simple steps from the BRRI brown spot factsheet, each
with its source, and a reminder to ask the agriculture office before using any chemical.

13
00:01:33,433 --> 00:01:41,212
When the photo is poor or the model is unsure, Kakatarua says: I am
not sure, and gives retake tips instead of guessing.

14
00:01:41,342 --> 00:01:50,802
Three photos of one disease in one division within a week create a
draft alert. A reviewer approves it before farmers see: possible outbreak, unverified.

15
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:06,020
Under the hood: photo in,
AI triage, retrieval, validated advice out.

16
00:02:06,149 --> 00:02:13,579
Contextual retrieval searches thirty-nine passages from nine BRRI
factsheets, each with an AI-written context line.

17
00:02:13,709 --> 00:02:21,058
A validator checks every citation and every number,
and our own MCP server exposes the same knowledge base to developers.

18
00:02:21,188 --> 00:02:29,268
Row-level security on Supabase, FastAPI on Render,
React on Vercel, and more than one thousand automated tests.

19
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:38,424
First live test: on five labelled field photos, both confident
answers were right, and all three wrong guesses were held back as not sure.

20
00:02:38,554 --> 00:02:45,879
Our targets: zero wrong advice shown, verified outbreak alerts
within a week, and fewer unnecessary sprays.

21
00:02:46,009 --> 00:02:54,608
Next: a labelled evaluation, agronomist review and
more crops, sponsored by cooperatives, NGOs and extension programmes.

22
00:02:54,738 --> 00:02:58,748
Kakatarua. Honest help for every rice field.
